      "id": 1,
      "claim": "\"Totally legal\" means an activity is not prohibited by criminal law; it may be regulated, but it is not merely tolerated while remaining illegal.",
      "evidence": "Legal principle: an act is legal if the penal code does not prescribe a sanction. De‑criminalisation or tolerance (gedoogbeleid) does not remove the statutory prohibition.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "claim": "Prostitution is legal in the Netherlands, subject to licensing and health‑safety regulations.",
      "evidence": "Sex Work Act (Wet regulering prostitutie), 2000, permits sex work as a regulated profession.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Euthanasia is legal in the Netherlands when strict medical criteria are met.",
      "evidence": "Termination of Life on Request and Assisted Suicide (Review Procedures) Act, 2002, allows physicians to perform euthanasia under due‑care criteria.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Cannabis and other soft drugs are not fully legal; they remain prohibited under the Opium Act, with possession up to 5 g only tolerated (a misdemeanor).",
      "evidence": "Opium Act classifies cannabis as a controlled substance; policy of gedoogbeleid permits limited possession and coffee‑shop sales but does not repeal the prohibition.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Hard drugs (e.g., heroin, cocaine) are illegal and punishable under the Opium Act.",
      "evidence": "Opium Act distinguishes hard drugs as prohibited substances with criminal penalties for possession and trafficking.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "claim": "Option C correctly states that prostitution and euthanasia are legal (with restrictions) and does not claim any drugs are legal.",
      "evidence": "Steps 2 and 3 confirm the legality of prostitution and euthanasia; step 4 shows drugs are not legal, so C avoids a false claim.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [2, 3, 4]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "claim": "All other options (A, B, D, E, F) assert that cannabis, soft drugs, or drugs in general are legal, contradicting step 4 (and step 5).",
      "evidence": "Step 4 shows soft drugs are only tolerated, not legal; step 5 shows hard drugs are illegal.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [4, 5]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "claim": "Therefore the correct answer is option C.",
      "evidence": "Step 6 identifies C as consistent with the law; step 7 eliminates all other options.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [6, 7]
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
